IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `au-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `au-part7-powers`
IMPORT `au-part7-more`

-- Tests for the provisions of Part 7 that pass 1 left unencoded. Expected values are written from the text, not from the program.
-- Calendar: 2026-02-28 is a Saturday, 2026-03-01 a Sunday, 2026-03-02 a Monday.

`no closures` MEANS `Days of closure` OF (LIST), (LIST)

`a closure on 2 March 2026` MEANS `Days of closure` OF (LIST), (LIST (Date 2 3 2026))

§ `Section 33(1)`

#ASSERT `what section 33(1) says is to be done` `a power` TRUE EQUALS `the power may be exercised`
#ASSERT `what section 33(1) says is to be done` `a function` TRUE EQUALS `the function must be performed`
#ASSERT `what section 33(1) says is to be done` `a duty` TRUE EQUALS `the duty must be performed`
-- "as occasion requires": when no occasion requires it, the subsection says nothing about the thing.
#ASSERT `what section 33(1) says is to be done` `a power` FALSE EQUALS `section 33(1) says nothing about it`
#ASSERT `what section 33(1) says is to be done` `a duty` FALSE EQUALS `section 33(1) says nothing about it`

§ `Section 33(2A)`

#ASSERT `the act or thing may be done at the discretion of the person, court or body` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An Act assented to before the subsection commenced, an Act that does not give a person, court or body a thing to do, or one that does
-- not use the word "may": the subsection says nothing.
#ASSERT `the act or thing may be done at the discretion of the person, court or body` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the act or thing may be done at the discretion of the person, court or body` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the act or thing may be done at the discretion of the person, court or body` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 33(2B)`

-- "Whether incorporated or unincorporated": the answer is the same either way.
#ASSERT `the exercise or performance is affected merely because of a vacancy in the membership` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the exercise or performance is affected merely because of a vacancy in the membership` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not conferred on a body, or a reason other than a vacancy: the subsection says nothing.
#ASSERT `the exercise or performance is affected merely because of a vacancy in the membership` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the exercise or performance is affected merely because of a vacancy in the membership` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 33(3) and (3AA)`

#ASSERT `the power to make the instrument includes the power to do this to it` TRUE `to repeal it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power to make the instrument includes the power to do this to it` TRUE `to rescind it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power to make the instrument includes the power to do this to it` TRUE `to revoke it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power to make the instrument includes the power to do this to it` TRUE `to amend it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power to make the instrument includes the power to do this to it` TRUE `to vary it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power to make the instrument includes the power to do this to it` TRUE `to do something else to it` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power to make the instrument includes the power to do this to it` FALSE `to repeal it` EQUALS NOTHING
-- 3AA, and its Example: the Minister may give a written permission if satisfied the person is of good character. That condition must be
-- satisfied before the giving and is capable of ceasing to be satisfied afterwards, so for repeal, rescission or revocation the
-- condition is the ongoing condition ceasing to be satisfied.
#ASSERT `the condition that governs doing this to the instrument` `to revoke it` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the ongoing condition ceasing to be satisfied`
#ASSERT `the condition that governs doing this to the instrument` `to repeal it` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the ongoing condition ceasing to be satisfied`
#ASSERT `the condition that governs doing this to the instrument` `to rescind it` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the ongoing condition ceasing to be satisfied`
-- 3AA speaks of repeal, rescission and revocation only: an amendment or variation keeps the like condition.
#ASSERT `the condition that governs doing this to the instrument` `to amend it` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the like condition`
#ASSERT `the condition that governs doing this to the instrument` `to vary it` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the like condition`
-- A condition that cannot cease to be satisfied, or that need not be satisfied before the making, is not an ongoing condition.
#ASSERT `the condition that governs doing this to the instrument` `to revoke it` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the like condition`
#ASSERT `the condition that governs doing this to the instrument` `to revoke it` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the like condition`
#ASSERT `the condition that governs doing this to the instrument` `to do something else to it` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 33(3A), (3AB), (3AC) and (3B)`

#ASSERT `the power includes making the instrument in this way` TRUE `with respect to some only of the matters` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power includes making the instrument in this way` TRUE `with respect to a particular class of the matters` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power includes making the instrument in this way` TRUE `with respect to particular classes of the matters` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power includes making the instrument in this way` TRUE `making different provision with respect to different matters` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power includes making the instrument in this way` TRUE `making different provision with respect to different classes of matters` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power includes making the instrument in this way` TRUE `in some other way as to matters` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power includes making the instrument in this way` FALSE `with respect to some only of the matters` EQUALS NOTHING
-- 3AB: legislative instruments, notifiable instruments and rules of court are excepted.
#ASSERT `the person or authority may identify the matter by reference to a class or classes of matters` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the person or authority may identify the matter by reference to a class or classes of matters` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the person or authority may identify the matter by reference to a class or classes of matters` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the person or authority may identify the matter by reference to a class or classes of matters` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the person or authority may identify the matter by reference to a class or classes of matters` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 3AC: matter includes thing, person and animal.
#ASSERT `it is a matter for subsections 33(3A) and 33(3AB)` `a thing that is a matter`
#ASSERT `it is a matter for subsections 33(3A) and 33(3AB)` `a person that is a matter`
#ASSERT `it is a matter for subsections 33(3A) and 33(3AB)` `an animal that is a matter`
#ASSERT `it is a matter for subsections 33(3A) and 33(3AB)` `something else that is a matter`
#ASSERT NOT (`it is a matter for subsections 33(3A) and 33(3AB)` `something that is not a matter`)
-- 3B.
#ASSERT `the power is taken, by implication, not to include power to make provision for a particular aspect of a matter` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the power is taken, by implication, not to include power to make provision for a particular aspect of a matter` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power is taken, by implication, not to include power to make provision for a particular aspect of a matter` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 33(4)`

#ASSERT `the power to make appointments includes this` TRUE `appointing a person to act in the office or place` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power to make appointments includes this` TRUE `removing a person appointed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power to make appointments includes this` TRUE `suspending a person appointed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power to make appointments includes this` TRUE `appointing another person temporarily in the place of a person suspended` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power to make appointments includes this` TRUE `appointing another person temporarily in the place of a sick or absent holder` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power to make appointments includes this` TRUE `something else about appointments` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power to make appointments includes this` FALSE `removing a person appointed` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The proviso: only the power to appoint to act and the power of removal are made subject to the other person's recommendation or consent.
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised as the proviso to section 33(4) requires` `appointing a person to act in the office or place` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised as the proviso to section 33(4) requires` `appointing a person to act in the office or place` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised as the proviso to section 33(4) requires` `removing a person appointed` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised as the proviso to section 33(4) requires` `removing a person appointed` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised as the proviso to section 33(4) requires` `suspending a person appointed` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised as the proviso to section 33(4) requires` `appointing another person temporarily in the place of a person suspended` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised as the proviso to section 33(4) requires` `removing a person appointed` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (a) and (b), whichever first happens. The office became vacant on 15 March 2026: the 12 months end on 15 March 2027.
#ASSERT `the day the acting appointment under section 33(4) ends` NOTHING (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 3 2027)
#ASSERT `the day the acting appointment under section 33(4) ends` (JUST (Date 1 6 2026)) (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 6 2026)
#ASSERT `the day the acting appointment under section 33(4) ends` (JUST (Date 15 3 2027)) (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 3 2027)
-- A person appointed after the 12 months have run does not lengthen them.
#ASSERT `the day the acting appointment under section 33(4) ends` (JUST (Date 1 1 2028)) (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 3 2027)

§ `Sections 33(5) and 33AA`

#ASSERT `the limit on penalties prevents the instrument from requiring a statutory declaration` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the limit on penalties prevents the instrument from requiring a statutory declaration` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the limit on penalties prevents the instrument from requiring a statutory declaration` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power to make the appointment includes a power of reappointment` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power to make the appointment includes a power of reappointment` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 33A (the paragraphs pass 1 left)`

-- (1): a provision other than s 33(4) that confers a power to appoint a person to act in an office, except so far as the Act otherwise provides.
#ASSERT `section 33A(1) applies to the appointment` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`section 33A(1) applies to the appointment` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`section 33A(1) applies to the appointment` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`section 33A(1) applies to the appointment` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- (a) and (b).
#ASSERT `the appointer may do this under section 33A(1)` TRUE `expressing the appointment to have effect only in the circumstances specified in the instrument of appointment`
#ASSERT `the appointer may do this under section 33A(1)` TRUE `determining the terms and conditions of the appointment, including remuneration and allowances`
#ASSERT `the appointer may do this under section 33A(1)` TRUE `terminating the appointment at any time`
#ASSERT NOT (`the appointer may do this under section 33A(1)` TRUE `something else about an acting appointment`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the appointer may do this under section 33A(1)` FALSE `terminating the appointment at any time`)
-- (d): resigns in writing delivered to the appointer.
#ASSERT `the appointment ceases to have effect on the appointee's resignation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the appointment ceases to have effect on the appointee's resignation` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the appointment ceases to have effect on the appointee's resignation` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the appointment ceases to have effect on the appointee's resignation` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the appointment ceases to have effect on the appointee's resignation` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- (e): while the appointee is acting.
#ASSERT `the appointee has this while acting in the office` TRUE TRUE `all the powers of the holder of the office`
#ASSERT `the appointee has this while acting in the office` TRUE TRUE `the functions and duties of the holder of the office`
#ASSERT `the appointee has this while acting in the office` TRUE TRUE `the application of the Act concerned or any other Act as if the person were the holder`
#ASSERT NOT (`the appointee has this while acting in the office` TRUE TRUE `something else the holder of the office has`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the appointee has this while acting in the office` TRUE FALSE `all the powers of the holder of the office`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the appointee has this while acting in the office` FALSE TRUE `all the powers of the holder of the office`)
-- (2): acting by operation of law.
#ASSERT `the person acting by operation of law has this while acting in the office` TRUE FALSE TRUE `all the powers of the holder of the office`
#ASSERT `the person acting by operation of law has this while acting in the office` TRUE FALSE TRUE `the functions and duties of the holder of the office`
#ASSERT `the person acting by operation of law has this while acting in the office` TRUE FALSE TRUE `the application of the Act concerned or any other Act as if the person were the holder`
#ASSERT NOT (`the person acting by operation of law has this while acting in the office` TRUE TRUE TRUE `all the powers of the holder of the office`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the person acting by operation of law has this while acting in the office` FALSE FALSE TRUE `all the powers of the holder of the office`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the person acting by operation of law has this while acting in the office` TRUE FALSE FALSE `all the powers of the holder of the office`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the person acting by operation of law has this while acting in the office` TRUE FALSE TRUE `something else the holder of the office has`)
-- (3): not invalid merely because the occasion to act had not arisen or had ceased.
#ASSERT `the thing done is invalid merely because of this ground for purported acting` TRUE `the occasion to act had not arisen` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the thing done is invalid merely because of this ground for purported acting` TRUE `the occasion to act had ceased` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the thing done is invalid merely because of this ground for purported acting` TRUE `some other ground about acting` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the thing done is invalid merely because of this ground for purported acting` FALSE `the occasion to act had ceased` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 33B`

-- (1): "whether or not incorporated".
#ASSERT `section 33B applies to the body` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `section 33B applies to the body` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`section 33B applies to the body` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`section 33B applies to the body` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- (2): telephone, closed-circuit television, any other means of communication.
#ASSERT `the body may permit its members to participate by this means` TRUE `telephone`
#ASSERT `the body may permit its members to participate by this means` TRUE `closed-circuit television`
#ASSERT `the body may permit its members to participate by this means` TRUE `any other means of communication`
#ASSERT NOT (`the body may permit its members to participate by this means` FALSE `telephone`)
-- (3): taken to be present and to form part of any quorum.
#ASSERT `the member is taken to be present at the meeting and to form part of any quorum` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the member is taken to be present at the meeting and to form part of any quorum` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the member is taken to be present at the meeting and to form part of any quorum` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the member is taken to be present at the meeting and to form part of any quorum` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- (4): all the members may participate by such a means.
#ASSERT `all the members may participate by this means` TRUE TRUE `telephone`
#ASSERT NOT (`all the members may participate by this means` TRUE FALSE `telephone`)
-- (5): two or more places at the same time.
#ASSERT `the meeting may be held at that number of places at the same time` TRUE TRUE 2 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the meeting may be held at that number of places at the same time` TRUE TRUE 3 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the meeting may be held at that number of places at the same time` TRUE TRUE 1 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the meeting may be held at that number of places at the same time` TRUE FALSE 2 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the meeting may be held at that number of places at the same time` FALSE TRUE 2 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Sections 34 and 34AAA`

#ASSERT `the person authorised to hear and determine the matter has authority to do this` `authority given by law` `to receive evidence` FALSE
#ASSERT `the person authorised to hear and determine the matter has authority to do this` `authority given by consent of the parties` `to examine witnesses` FALSE
#ASSERT `the person authorised to hear and determine the matter has authority to do this` `authority given by law` `to administer an oath or affirmation to a witness` TRUE
-- The oath or affirmation is to witnesses "legally called before them".
#ASSERT NOT (`the person authorised to hear and determine the matter has authority to do this` `authority given by law` `to administer an oath or affirmation to a witness` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the person authorised to hear and determine the matter has authority to do this` `no authority to hear and determine the matter` `to receive evidence` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the person authorised to hear and determine the matter has authority to do this` `authority given by law` `to do something else at the hearing` TRUE)
#ASSERT `the person who exercises the power or performs the function or duty` TRUE "the Secretary for the time being" EQUALS JUST "the Secretary for the time being"
#ASSERT `the person who exercises the power or performs the function or duty` FALSE "the Secretary for the time being" EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 34AAB`

-- (1): a Minister who does not administer the Act or provision, or a member of the Executive Council who is not a Minister.
#ASSERT `the Minister may authorise this person to act on the Minister's behalf` TRUE `a Minister who does not administer the Act or provision`
#ASSERT `the Minister may authorise this person to act on the Minister's behalf` TRUE `a member of the Executive Council who is not a Minister`
#ASSERT NOT (`the Minister may authorise this person to act on the Minister's behalf` TRUE `a Minister who administers the Act or provision`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the Minister may authorise this person to act on the Minister's behalf` TRUE `any other person`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the Minister may authorise this person to act on the Minister's behalf` FALSE `a Minister who does not administer the Act or provision`)
-- (2): functions under an instrument having effect under the Act are covered too.
#ASSERT `the authorisation extends to the function, duty or power` `the Act or provision` TRUE
#ASSERT `the authorisation extends to the function, duty or power` `an instrument having effect under or for the purposes of the Act or provision` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the authorisation extends to the function, duty or power` `a source outside the Act or provision and its instruments` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the authorisation extends to the function, duty or power` `the Act or provision` FALSE)
-- (3).
#ASSERT `an authorisation may be expressed in this way` `to have effect only during a period or periods`
#ASSERT `an authorisation may be expressed in this way` `to have effect only during the existence of a circumstance or circumstances`
#ASSERT `an authorisation may be expressed in this way` `to take effect immediately and afterwards continue until another person is appointed to the office held by the authorising Minister`
#ASSERT `an authorisation may be expressed in this way` `to take effect at a time referred to in the authorisation and afterwards continue until another person is appointed to the office held by the authorising Minister`
#ASSERT NOT (`an authorisation may be expressed in this way` `to be expressed in some other way`)
#ASSERT `the authorisation continues to have effect` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`the authorisation continues to have effect` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the authorisation continues to have effect` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the authorisation continues to have effect` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (4): revoked at any time by the authorising Minister.
#ASSERT `the authorisation may be revoked at any time` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the authorisation may be revoked at any time` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the authorisation may be revoked at any time` FALSE TRUE)
-- (5): in writing.
#ASSERT `it complies with subsection 34AAB(5)` `an authorisation under subsection 34AAB(1)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `it complies with subsection 34AAB(5)` `an authorisation under subsection 34AAB(1)` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `it complies with subsection 34AAB(5)` `the revocation of such an authorisation` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `it complies with subsection 34AAB(5)` `the revocation of such an authorisation` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `it complies with subsection 34AAB(5)` `something that is neither` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (6).
#ASSERT `section 34AAB stops the giving of an authorisation under that other power` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `section 34AAB stops the giving of an authorisation under that other power` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Sections 34AA and 34AB`

#ASSERT `the power of delegation includes delegating to a delegate described in this way` TRUE `a specified person` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power of delegation includes delegating to a delegate described in this way` TRUE `any person from time to time holding the specified office or position` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power of delegation includes delegating to a delegate described in this way` TRUE `any person from time to time holding the specified office or position` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power of delegation includes delegating to a delegate described in this way` TRUE `any person from time to time occupying the specified office or position` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power of delegation includes delegating to a delegate described in this way` TRUE `any person from time to time performing the duties of the specified office or position` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power of delegation includes delegating to a delegate described in this way` TRUE `some other description of a delegate` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power of delegation includes delegating to a delegate described in this way` FALSE `a specified person` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 34AB(1).
#ASSERT `the delegation may be made in this way` TRUE `the delegation is made generally` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the delegation may be made in this way` TRUE `the delegation is made as otherwise provided by the instrument of delegation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the delegation may be made in this way` TRUE `the delegation is made in some other way` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the delegation may be made in this way` FALSE `the delegation is made generally` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power to delegate is among the powers that may be delegated` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the power to delegate is among the powers that may be delegated` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `for the purposes of the Act it is deemed to have been performed or exercised by the authority` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`for the purposes of the Act it is deemed to have been performed or exercised by the authority` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`for the purposes of the Act it is deemed to have been performed or exercised by the authority` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the delegation prevents the authority from performing or exercising the function, duty or power` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the delegation prevents the authority from performing or exercising the function, duty or power` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the delegation prevents the authority from performing or exercising the function, duty or power` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `section 34A applies to the authority as if it were a person` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`section 34A applies to the authority as if it were a person` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`section 34A applies to the authority as if it were a person` FALSE FALSE)
-- 34AB(2): "on and after the amendment taking effect": the day it takes effect is included.
#ASSERT NOT (`the delegation is taken to include the additional functions, duties or powers on this day` TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 30 6 2026))
#ASSERT `the delegation is taken to include the additional functions, duties or powers on this day` TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 1 7 2026)
#ASSERT `the delegation is taken to include the additional functions, duties or powers on this day` TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 2 7 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (`the delegation is taken to include the additional functions, duties or powers on this day` FALSE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 2 7 2026))
#ASSERT NOT (`the delegation is taken to include the additional functions, duties or powers on this day` TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 2 7 2026))
#ASSERT NOT (`the delegation is taken to include the additional functions, duties or powers on this day` TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 2 7 2026))
-- 34AB(3).
#ASSERT NOT (`the delegation is taken to include the functions, duties or powers as altered on this day` TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 30 6 2026))
#ASSERT `the delegation is taken to include the functions, duties or powers as altered on this day` TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 1 7 2026)
#ASSERT `the delegation is taken to include the functions, duties or powers as altered on this day` TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 1 1 2027)
#ASSERT NOT (`the delegation is taken to include the functions, duties or powers as altered on this day` FALSE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 2 7 2026))
#ASSERT NOT (`the delegation is taken to include the functions, duties or powers as altered on this day` TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 2 7 2026))
#ASSERT NOT (`the delegation is taken to include the functions, duties or powers as altered on this day` TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 2 7 2026))

